      "why": "Genetic testing identified a heterozygous KRT6A c.1460-2_1460del variant that is absent in both parents, confirming a de novo mutation diagnostic of Pachyonychia congenita, a congenital hereditary keratoderma. The clinical triad of nail dystrophy, palmoplantar hyperkeratosis, and oral leukokeratosis matches this diagnosis. Pathologist and laboratory physician analyses agree that molecular confirmation is sufficient even without skin biopsy, so confidence rises from 0.75 to 0.98."
